  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "app-name",
      "lines": [
        "The app name Element for Nextcloud in appinfo/info.xml uses Nextcloud.",
        "  The App Store publishing rules say apps must not use Nextcloud in their name; a name that does reads as an app of Nextcloud itself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 28 to 31; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  max-version 31 is below the oldest maintained major (32, as of 2026-09), so the release covers only servers that no longer receive fixes.",
        "  min-version 28 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "php-extensions",
      "lines": [
        "1 PHP extension is required by composer but not listed as <lib> in appinfo/info.xml:",
        "  tokenizer (kubawerlos/php-cs-fixer-custom-fixers, php-cs-fixer/shim)",
        "  A Nextcloud server need not load it. The server checks <lib> before it enables the app; composer only checks where it runs. Without the <lib> the app is enabled anyway and the first call into the extension fails at runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "3rdparty/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Controller/StaticController.php:102 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += 3rdparty ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 20 stated in .nvmrc.",
        "  Not stated in engines.node in package.json, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (./src/.eslintrc.json), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), EditorConfig (.editorconfig).",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHPUnit configuration: there is no test harness in the checkout, so nothing can be run against a change.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: vue-template-compiler.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 3,155 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json, composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
      "lines": [
        "Version 0.19.0 in appinfo/info.xml and package.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    }
